  {
   "id": "forever",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "b09",
     "say": "Here's the first thing."
    },
    {
     "id": "b10",
     "say": "A tattoo isn't really a decision about today."
    },
    {
     "id": "b11",
     "say": "It's a decision about every version of you that comes after today."
    },
    {
     "id": "b12",
     "say": "And psychologists have found something strange about how we see those future versions."
    },
    {
     "id": "b13",
     "say": "In a 2013 study, people of every age said they'd changed a lot over the past ten years…"
    },
    {
     "id": "b14",
     "say": "but expected to change very little over the next ten."
    },
    {
     "id": "b15",
     "say": "Researchers called it the \"end of history illusion.\""
    },
    {
     "id": "b16",
     "say": "Most of us believe who we are right now is who we'll always be."
    },
    {
     "id": "b17",
     "say": "People who don't get tattoos often have a quiet suspicion that this isn't true."
    },
    {
     "id": "b18",
     "say": "They can feel that their future self might not agree."
    },
    {
     "id": "b19",
     "say": "So they don't sign a contract on that person's behalf."
    }
   ],
